  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Genesis Lotus’ will wears a green and white robe. He has a gentle demeanor and a smile on his face.",
      "chapters": [
        2082
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan first meets the name on the Flower Wine Monk inheritance path while learning the background of Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus, where the recipe is tied to a righteous faction Gu Master from many millenniums earlier.",
      "chapters": [
        163
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_flower_wine_monk",
        "gu_heavenly_essence_treasure_lotus",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later narration classes only rank nine Gu Masters as venerables, names Immortal Venerable for the righteous path and Demonic Venerable for the demonic path, and ranks him as the person with the fastest primeval essence recovery since ancient times, above other Immortal and Demonic Venerables, because of the Essence Lotus.",
      "chapters": [
        187
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At a Shang clan city auction, Gu Masters call the rank three to rank five Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus line his core Gu, and say that refining rank six Heavenly Essence Treasure Imperial Lotus is rumored to open his inheritance ground.",
      "chapters": [
        308
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Gu world, rank nine is Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        187
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Venerable names a rank nine righteous Gu Master; Demon Venerable names a rank nine demonic path Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        383
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_righteous_path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Essence Treasure Imperial Lotus is a rank six Immortal Gu invented by him rather than found as a natural Gu. Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus at rank three, Heavenly Essence Treasure Monarch Lotus at rank four, and Heavenly Essence Treasure King Lotus at rank five produce primeval essence; Imperial Lotus at rank six and above produces immortal essence. He relied on that Gu to become the person with the most abundant immortal essence among rank nine Gu Immortals in history. After he died, the Imperial Lotus was guarded as a famous treasure until the later Venerable who became the heavenly thief, Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable, stole it as a rank seven Gu Immortal.",
      "chapters": [
        463
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "imperial-lotus-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_gu_venerable",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later crystal-wall description again calls the full series his creation and names Imperial Lotus sixth among the top ten Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        558
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "imperial-lotus-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is named a wood path rank nine Gu Venerable, and a land spirit ownership condition asks for his fresh blood, treated as a rank nine immortal material that might still be preserved by Heavenly Lotus Sect.",
      "chapters": [
        897
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wood-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later historical summary names him the creator of wood path and the owner of Heavenly Essence Treasure Imperial Lotus.",
      "chapters": [
        1235
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wood-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Another Medieval Antiquity Era summary again credits him with creating wood path. The same summary credits Thieving Heaven with theft path and Giant Sun with luck path.",
      "chapters": [
        1323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wood-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_era_medieval"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rank eight Immortal Gu House Heavenly Pool is the base of Heavenly Lotus Sect, created by him, and its greatest use is to store immortal apertures. Talk during an attack on that house says that among the ten venerables he was most specialized in healing and recovery, and that Heavenly Pool inherits that style so strongly that anything short of a total break can recover severe losses quickly.",
      "chapters": [
        1000
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-house-legacy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "loc_heavenly_pool"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black Extremity tells Flood Extremity that perseverance Immortal Gu is real rather than only a legend from The Legends of Ren Zu, and that its refiner was the famous Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable, who entered the door of life and death, brought Reverse Flow River out into the world, and became its first owner.",
      "chapters": [
        1277
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "perseverance-gu-and-reverse-flow-river",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_sun_ming_lu",
        "char_flood_extremity",
        "gu_perseverance_gu",
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
        "loc_reverse_flow_river"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wei Ling Yang names him a former leader of Heavenly Court and the person who had once owned perseverance Immortal Gu. The immemorial desolate beast Mao Li Qiu says Genesis Lotus charged into Reverse Flow River and was trapped there, and refined perseverance Immortal Gu in his body only after painstakingly reaching the river’s end, conquering the river and becoming the first Reverse Flow River Lord in history.",
      "chapters": [
        1285
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-and-heavenly-lotus-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wei_ling_yang",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_mao_li_qiu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later text states that Central Continent’s Heavenly Lotus Sect was created by him, and that during his era the sect was the number one sect in Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        1522
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-and-heavenly-lotus-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Medieval Antiquity Era, three hundred thousand years before the present, Genesis Lotus, Thieving Heaven, and Giant Sun appear in succession.",
      "chapters": [
        1867
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-era",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A late roster of the Ten Venerables places him in that same era beside Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable and Giant Sun Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        2085
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-era",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    }
  ],
